    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d390-a3">

                <pb facs="0567" n="471" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg471"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3 in No. 228.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Herod to the Director of the Patent Bureau.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1898-11-28"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">November 28,
                    1898</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Yanagiya</hi>: With reference to the
                    conversation I had with you on Saturday regarding the trade-mark of the New York
                    Condensed Milk Company, I send you herewith one of the papers in the <pb
                        facs="0568" n="472" xml:id="pg472"/> case setting out that the application
                    for registration is numbered 12092, and was presented to your department by one
                    S. Nukiyama.</p>
                <p>Kindly return the paper when you have finished.</p>
                <p>Sincerely, yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Joseph R. Herod.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
